  <title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01844</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3caa4f45-a25a-44ee-acdc-c6a1a0e6bdc0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>This graph represents the revenue in dollars that a company expects if they sell their product for \(p\) dollars.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of non linear function.&quot; height=&quot;196"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4b5d552eb1fbfb0822e47b7883a920ba6c68d147"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Based on this model, which price would generate more revenue for the company, \($5\) or \($17\)?</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \($5\), as it would generate about \($3,700\) in revenue. Charging \($17\) would bring in about \($2,500\).</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>At what price (in dollars) should the company sell their product if they wish to make as much revenue as possible?</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(10\)</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>How much revenue (in dollars) would they make?</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(5,000\)</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is an appropriate domain for the function? Explain how you know.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. </para>
</list></section>
</content>
